I decided before this game started that I was after two quest
artifacts, The Eye of the Aethiopica and the Staff of Aesculapius.
I also wanted to keep a few conducts (vegan, polyselfless, and
polyobjectless).

The early portion of the game was mostly unremarkable.  The dungeon
featured two early bookstores, sokoban had reflection, and Izchak was
short on candles.  Minetown did have a magic marker, and a bones pile
in the bottom half of the mines netted a quarterstaff and cloak of
magic resistance.  Mines end was the catacombs.

Being only In:09, reading spellbooks was still a risky proposition.
A failed attempt convinced me to defer reading books until the mid-
to-late-game.  I arrived at the Castle T:16397 with HP:88(88), AC:-11
and knowing one spell (sleep) to be greeted by a teleporting master
lich.

After dealing with the big L, it was tooled horn concerto time.
Most of the audience got drawbridged.  I let a disenchanter out so
I could hit it with some wielded armour.  After that I charged
inside, only to find a titan in the throne room.  I danced around it
without facing too severe a summon storm and got the wand of wishing.
It was quite helpfully a (0:3) wand, meaning the two-quest-artifact
strategy was a "conditional go"

The first three wishes were spent on 2 blessed scrolls of charging,
the Eye of the Aethiopica, and a bag of holding.  After enchanting my
armour and quarterstaff (dumb, in retrospect), I wanted to check the
store rooms before eyeporting to Sokoban and planning my next move.
The Titan had other ideas.  After botching the encounter, I did an
emergency eyeport out of there.

In Sokoban, I had a study session while I healed.  Here I had a brain
fart, and went exploring for a level or so before remembering TEH
PLAN: wish up Staff (and a spellbook of summon sacrifice^W^Wcreate
monster), altarcamp for a few spellbooks and a !GL, get crowned, then
go quest.

Along the way, Vorpy landed at my feet (it went snicker-snack :).

The monk quest wasn't as brutal as I remembered (sleep is the key).
In the locate level, I failed to read 'create familiar'.  The many
many --more-- messages left me cursing my stupid.

Upon reaching Kaen's lair, I (being fast and invisible) decided to do
a bit of exploring before tackling Kaen.  Two steps later, a big,
purple @ forced an episode of "all stop, full reverse, DON'T PRESS
KEYS!"  After calming down a bit, I cast sleep at Kaen, then level-
drained him with the Staff of Aesculapius.  After each hit, I applied
a stethoscope.  The patient never woke up.

I walked back to the Castle, drawbridged the Titan, checked the store
rooms (no artifacts, thankfully), then it was time to tackle the
Valley of the Dead and the rest of Gehennom.

I tried (and failed) to rip off Asmodeus.  Then I figured I'd hog the
downstairs and decapitate him with Vorpy.  Eventually I got bored
with waiting for him to teleport back to me (he ran away after every
hit, and food can become an issue for a vegan spellcaster) and did
the downstair/upstair trick.  Baalzebub was paid off for the princely
sum of two zorkmids.  Juiblex was battered to death while I never
left the upstair.  I bypassed Orcus town, coming up from below.
Orcus never used his wand, but a shade managed to steal my speed.

After killing Orcus, the gloves came off, a silver ring went on,
and "cdi was kung-fu fighting!  His fists moved fast as lightning!"
While cleaning out Orcus-town, I named one of my lizard corpses
"This is a YAESD waiting to happen" (gloveless, using kung-fu, and
haven't genocided 'c').

Somewhere along the way, someone gated in Yeenoghu and I spent my
last non-wrest wish on a ring of teleport.

After marking the Vibrating Square, I eyeported back to the Castle
and did one final round of inventory (mis)management.  I noticed I
was short on means portal detection.  This meant, barring an
emergency during the run, I would be wresting for an uncursed magic
marker just before hitting the elemental planes.

I levelported down to the wizards tower entrance level, and climbed
through the zoo hoping for a 'c' corpse along the way.  Two left
corpses (Allen and Fred).  Allen made this nice statue of the
Wizard of Yendor (such the artist!).

Next came a levelport to the Vibrating Square, followed by my 2nd
favorite ritual.  I stepped downstairs, then back up before level-
porting down again (landed on the left).  Allen made several more
statues, including this really pretty one of the High Priest of
Moloch.  After grabbing the Amulet, the race was on.

The ascension run was mostly uneventful, except for Rodney's first
appearance.  I was midway through Juiblex' swamp when he re-appeared.
The Wand of Orcus missed from point-blank range FOUR TIMES.  During
all of this, Rodney stole the Eyes of the Overworld and the Amulet
of Yendor.  I had no pick-axe, so losing the Eyes in water was not an
option.  I had to be very careful and only hit Rodney when he wasn't
over water.  Eventually he ported to the stairs.  I level-ported up
one, came downstairs, and level-drained Rodney to death with the
Staff of Aesculapius.

I managed to make it all the way up to Dlvl.01 without any other
(non-mysterious force related) annoyances.  I was about 4 steps
away from the upstair when "Oh, hi there Rodney."  I skipped my
usual inventory re-arrangement routine and went up once I wouldn't
be followed.

Before leaving Earth for Air, I engrave-wrested my wand of wishing
for an uncursed magic marker without putting time on the clock and
wrote enough c?confuse monster and ?gold detection to get me to
Astral.

For reasons related to hostile angel placement, I chose to go
center->right->left on the Astral plane despite arriving on the left.
The central altar was guarded by Pesty.  Here I made a (potentially
fatal) tactical error.  Thinking I had a free move coming, and
knowing I needed no more than two hits to drop Pesty, I chose melee
instead of zapping a /death.  I was wrong.  Ill and Stun while next
to Pestilence is a good way to die.

/* aside: IMO, Pesty, Famine, and Demogorgon were less dangerous
   when their second successful touch attack resulted in stacked
   illness/hunger instead of stunning (as it does now). */

The center altar was Lawful, and on the way out someone else killed
Pestilence (go team conflict!).  Some careful maneuvering on the
way to the right altar and I avoided Famine all together.  This was
the neutral altar.  Off came conflict, had a little chat with the
High Priest (I got two bits), and then #offered.

-cdi, who snipped the endgame dump to suit his own nefarious purposes.
